course: dictionary
lesson: 15824
title: Undamaged
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Undamaged is built from two parts. The un- means not, and damaged means harmed or broken. So undamaged means not harmed or broken, and still in good condition.
explain: «The plate fell off the table, but it was undamaged.» The word «fell» tells you the plate could have broken. «But» shows that it did not, so undamaged must mean not broken.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The plate fell off the table, but it was not harmed or broken.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Look out for phrases. To escape undamaged means to get away from danger without being hurt. To be left undamaged means to be kept in good condition.
fact: Undamaged is an adjective, a word that describes a noun.
fact: «Undamaged» means not harmed or broken, and still in good condition.
fact: The prefix un- means not, as in «unhappy» and «unlock».
fact: «Escape undamaged» means get away from danger without being harmed.
fact: In shops, undamaged goods are goods that are not broken, so they can often be returned.
exercise: «The box arrived at my door, and the glass inside was still undamaged.» What does undamaged mean here? | Wrapped in paper | Very old and dusty | Full of water | *Not broken and in good condition
exercise: «The bridge was damaged in the flood, but the new one is undamaged.» Find and copy the one word that means not harmed. | flood | *undamaged | bridge | new
exercise: Ben says undamaged means covered in dents. What does it really mean? | Wet and muddy | Covered in dents | Very loud | *Not harmed or broken
test: «The cat jumped from the wall and landed undamaged.» What does undamaged mean? | Hurt and bruised | Painted | Asleep | *Not harmed
test: Why can the shop take back the undamaged jumper? | It is too small for everyone | It has a hole in it | *It is still in good condition and not broken | It was worn at the beach
exam: Which phrase means got away from danger without being harmed? | *Escape undamaged | Left undamaged | Stood in the rain | Lost in the storm
